# Project Rules & Standards

## Precision and Scope Control
- **Don't change things everywhere just because they are similar.** 
- **Only change what the user specifically asks for.**
- **Never modify .env files.** The user will handle environmental configurations.
- **Wait for explicit instruction before applying similar changes to other parts of the codebase.**
- **Priority: Avoid side effects.** "One thing changes and other places break" must be avoided by strictly limiting the scope of edits.

## Enterprise Standards (BlueHub)
- ASP.NET Core MVC (.NET 8)
- Entity Framework Core + Dapper
- Repository + Unit of Work pattern
- Layered architecture: EDContext, EDModels, EDRepository, EDService, EDUtility
- MSSQL database with 1000+ tables
- Heavy use of Razor views, Bootstrap 5, jQuery, DataTables
- Multi-language resource system (LangResx)
- Financial modules compatible with Turkish Uniform Chart of Accounts
- Maritime, Purchasing, Finance, Logistics, PMS, and Personnel modules

## Documentation Standards
- Standardized page titles (formtitle)
- Premium Upsert Modal Structure (modal-rule)
- KPI cards with right-side icon (cardrighticon)
